  <section>
    <h2>Project Overview</h2>
    <p>Built and deployed a machine learning classification model on Azure that predicts poor voice call quality. Call quality is measured by the Mean Opinion Score (MOS), a 1–5 scale of how users rate a call. The model uses network and call data to flag calls that need inspection.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Label</th><th>Condition</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>MOS ≥ 3</td><td>Good voice quality, no action needed</td></tr>
      <tr class="highlight"><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>MOS &lt; 3</td><td>Poor voice quality, needs inspection</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>Each flagged call is mapped to the <strong>serving cell (cell_id)</strong> that carried it. A dashboard ranks cells from the highest to the lowest number of label 1 calls. This turns thousands of call-level predictions into a short, prioritized list of network locations to fix.</p>
    <p>The model trained on <span class="est">~12M</span> historical call records and scores <span class="est">~400K</span> calls per day across <span class="est">~2,500</span> cells.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Key Features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Poor-quality call detection:</strong> Classifies each call as good (0) or needs inspection (1), with a tuned probability threshold.</li>
      <li><strong>Cell-level ranking:</strong> Maps each call to its serving cell_id and ranks cells by the count of label 1 calls, so engineers start with the cells that affect the most users.</li>
      <li><strong>Network-aware features:</strong> Uses jitter, packet loss, latency, codec, network type, device type, cell load and time of day.</li>
      <li><strong>Explainable drivers:</strong> Feature importance shows the top causes of poor quality, such as packet loss or peak-hour congestion.</li>
      <li><strong>Built for imbalance:</strong> Poor calls are only <span class="est">~11%</span> of traffic. Class weights and threshold tuning keep the model focused on finding them.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloud deployment:</strong> Model hosted on Azure, with daily batch scoring and results sent to the monitoring dashboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Monitoring &amp; retraining:</strong> Tracks recall, precision and data drift. Triggers retraining when performance drops below set limits.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

